2. microduck-lab — Jonathan Hawkins
   https://github.com/jonathanhawkins/microduck-lab
   Apache License 2.0

   Provides microduck_local (the CPU MuJoCo + PPO harness and the duck-lab
   server) and duck-viewer (the browser front end).

   MODIFICATION: this image adds a --host flag to duck-lab's argument parser
   so the server can bind inside a container's network namespace. The default
   remains 127.0.0.1 and the origin checks are untouched; see the comment in
   the Dockerfile for why this preserves upstream's loopback trust boundary.

3. MicroDuckModels — IronSpiderMan
   https://github.com/IronSpiderMan/MicroDuckModels
   The pretrained .onnx policies in /app/policies. Upstream states that these
   assets originate from Pollen Robotics' MicroDuck Simulator Space and asks
   that the upstream project's license terms be followed; they are therefore
   treated here as NON-COMMERCIAL, as in (1).

4. Third-party Python and JavaScript dependencies are installed from PyPI and
